II. INVARIANT FILTERING BASICS
FOR IMU BASED LOCALIZATION
The objective is to reproduce the position and orientation of an IMU in the global inertial frame over time against noises. The key step in optimal filtering, e.g., Kalman filter, is to derive the Riccati equation that governs how the covariance matrix, denoted by Σ, propagates [24]. To derive the Riccati equation, it is required that the state of the filter is governed by linear dynamics. This is possible if we reformulate the estimation problem using error state (ES) with the aid of matrix Lie group.
