V. SENSITIVITY ANALYSIS
The traditional EKF strongly depends on carefully tuned process noise covariance σω, σa for process and measurement noise, which are typically determined through extensive experimental data or statistical analysis. Variations in these covariance values can significantly degrade EKF performance [17]. In contrast, InEKF exhibits much less sensitivity to process covariance σω, σa and is therefore much easier to tune [18]. This is confirmed with sensitivity analysis experiment shown in Fig. 8. In Fig. 8a, both methods produce nearly


 7
identical trajectories when process noise covariance values are well-calibrated. Fig. 8b, 8c and 8d show the trajectory with detuned process noise covariance with a scaling of 10. It is observed that EKF trajectory begins to drift significantly, while the influence to the InEKF trajectory is mild. One can conclude that InEKF is less sensitive to parameters of process noise covariance σw and σa.
